  "notes": "Tutorial: Bird & Nest Messaging\n\nBIRDS carry messages to their NEST.\nThey work like a mailbox system!\n\nTHE SETUP:\n- The blue bird is paired with the nest\n- Anything given to the bird goes to the nest\n- The nest collects messages in order (FIFO)\n\nWATCH THE DEMO (click 'Show Me'):\n\n1. DRAG A NUMBER TO THE BIRD:\n   The bird carries it to the nest\n\n2. SEND ANOTHER NUMBER:\n   Messages queue up in order\n\n3. INSPECT WITH MAGNIFIER:\n   See the FIFO queue contents!\n\nTRY IT YOURSELF:\n- Drag numbers onto the bird\n- Use magnifier to inspect the nest\n- Click the nest to retrieve messages\n- Notice: first in = first out!\n\nUSE CASES:\n- Communication between robots\n- Collecting results over time\n- Asynchronous message passing",
  "notes_position": { "x": 480, "y": 60 },
  "notes_size": [380, 480],
